Crashes in upon my dreams.
The banns were read, my frock was sewn;
Since then two seasons' winds have blown--

over and up and on;
over and all is sewn;
now while I bind the end,

sew:
Nay, this thing will I do, while my mother tarrieth,
I will take my fine spun gold, but not to sew therewith,
I will take my gold and gems, and rainbow fan and wreath;

Naught to me like Dinah's arms;
Girls may draw, or paint, or sew--
I love Dinah kneading dough.

